---
description: Fail loud — prefer nil and tagged errors over empty-string defaults
alwaysApply: true
---

# Fail loud

Prefer `nil` and `{:error, reason}` over inventing a valid-looking empty string.

```elixir
# BAD — missing becomes "", then a second check
title = params |> Map.get("title", "") |> String.trim()
if title == "", do: flash, else: save(title)

# GOOD — changeset or pattern match; blank is nil
title = params["title"] |> blank_to_nil()
changeset = Song.changeset(%Song{}, %{title: title, artist: artist})
```

Do not swallow `{:error, _}` by returning the previous struct:

```elixir
# BAD
{:error, _} -> song

# GOOD
{:error, reason} -> {:error, reason}
```

Keep `with` and pattern matching on the happy path. Unknown error atoms must not become `"Something went wrong"` without a log. In `:dev`, raise.
